<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Nullroute — power and data policy exemptions.
    Installs to /system_ext/etc/sysconfig/sysconfig-nullroute.xml

    This file is the single largest reason to be an in-tree system_ext app rather
    than a sideloaded APK. Every off-store blocker spends its life fighting Doze,
    app standby buckets and the data saver, and loses quietly: the blocklist goes
    stale, the user never finds out, and the product silently degrades into
    whatever was current the week they installed it.

    None of these exemptions put the app in the DNS path. The path is netd + an
    mmap'd file; the app is a compiler and a UI that runs a few times a week.

    allow-in-power-save
        The refresh job (JobScheduler, ~daily) and the HealthWatchdog need to run
        while the device is idle. Without this the refresh lands only when the
        user happens to unlock during a maintenance window, which on a lightly
        used device can be never. The watchdog also has to clear
        persist.sys.nullroute.fail_streak after 120 s of healthy uptime — the
        boot-loop breaker (F7) counts a boot as bad if that never happens, so a
        Doze-suppressed watchdog would eventually quarantine a perfectly good
        index on the third boot.

    allow-in-data-usage-save
        Blocklist refreshes are conditional and small (Range version probe, then
        If-None-Match / If-Modified-Since, gzip or br). They must still be able
        to complete under Data Saver, because the alternative is an out-of-date
        malware list on exactly the connection the user was worried about.

    hidden-api-whitelisted-app
        The app is built against system_current, not platform_apis, so it uses
        no @hide API on the normal path. This entry exists so that the
        diagnostics bundle and the Deep-mode tunnel plumbing can reach the
        handful of greylisted members they need without the app having to be
        rebuilt against platform_apis — which would break the Gradle parity
        build that doubles as the stock-Android Deep-mode variant.

    NOT PRESENT, on purpose:
      * <allow-unthrottled-location> / any location exemption — Nullroute never
        touches location.
      * <allow-ignore-location-settings> — same.
      * <bugreport-whitelisted> — the diagnostics bundle is explicit and
        user-initiated; it does not need to ride along in every bug report.
-->
<config>
    <allow-in-power-save package="com.bestrom.nullroute" />
    <allow-in-data-usage-save package="com.bestrom.nullroute" />
    <hidden-api-whitelisted-app package="com.bestrom.nullroute" />
</config>
